cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research repository or its computational materials,
  please cite the repository. A permanent publication citation may be
  added after the associated manuscript or archival release is issued.
title: >-
  Cardiovascular Machine Learning Research:
  BRFSS-Based Classification of Prevalent Self-Reported
  Myocardial Infarction and Coronary Heart Disease with
  Temporal Validation
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhandari
    given-names: Keshav
repository-code: https://github.com/imksav/cardiovascular-ml-research
url: https://github.com/imksav/cardiovascular-ml-research
license: MIT
keywords:
  - BRFSS
  - cardiovascular machine learning
  - myocardial infarction
  - coronary heart disease
  - temporal validation
  - cross-sectional classification
  - reproducible research
  - calibration
abstract: >-
  Reproducible classification of prevalent self-reported myocardial
  infarction and/or coronary heart disease using BRFSS 2023, including
  held-out testing and frozen-pipeline evaluation on BRFSS 2025.
  Computational materials cover model comparison, calibration,
  survey-weighted evaluation point estimates, permutation feature
  importance and robustness analysis. This is not prospective event
  prediction or clinical validation.
